  "discussions_data": [
    {
      "id": "01f4909c09436c12de07973a76bee5a5f77847b2",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 576780270,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Not entirely sure the suggested fix is correct, topic is passed into the dissector in the data parameter as it's not part of the MQTT payload that's passed as the tvb which is then passed verbatim into the protobuf dissector.\n\nI should try to determine exactly what the minimum size of a sparkplugB message is.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6621762,
            "username": "graham.bloice",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Graham Bloice",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/8730bfac2267cb97ff1f8187d285f244745a03a783055c8fd6fcd679bfa71c6e?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/graham.bloice"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-05-17T11:06:24.531Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-05-17T11:06:24.531Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 100154947,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 3025,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "91a4832227ac16d2c543eba8d696251be7045a39",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 576807001,
          "type": null,
          "body": "It seems that all message types bar STATE will have a protobuf encoding of a sequence number.  STATE will have a non-protobuf UTF-8 string that should be handled locally and not handed off to the protobuf dissector.\nI'll have to generate a complete set of messages and check.\n\nI'm not sure how the issue is presented, but I'm assuming the fuzzing generated a capture with a zero length payload.  Shouldn't that cause the protobuf dissector to generate a dissector error?",
          "author": {
            "id": 6621762,
            "username": "graham.bloice",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Graham Bloice",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/8730bfac2267cb97ff1f8187d285f244745a03a783055c8fd6fcd679bfa71c6e?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/graham.bloice"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-05-17T11:21:47.959Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-05-17T11:21:47.959Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 100154947,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 3025,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "60712dbbf8af8d4bd4c2a7d2553c0ce3ceeefc56",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 576842111,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> I'm not sure how the issue is presented, but I'm assuming the fuzzing generated a capture with a zero length payload. Shouldn't that cause the protobuf dissector to generate a dissector error?\n\nYou're assuming it correct. However, any packet under 7 bytes would cause an error, since the code unconditionally runs g_strsplit and then uses the first token for a string comparison of 7 bytes.\n\nThe leak fix, on the other hand, should be fine, then I'm splitting them up.",
          "author": {
            "id": 277876,
            "username": "crondaemon",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Dario Lombardo",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/143ae7a6f9e11c9eed24a7fdb44bb40d442fd274ba01a2e3a4abe1596819bea2?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/crondaemon"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-05-17T11:50:18.538Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-05-17T11:50:18.538Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 100154947,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 3025,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4ad625a67bed636b5b04f8d089d26cd9b262783c",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 576844876,
          "type": null,
          "body": "added 2 commits\n\n<ul><li>8d9824bf - spakplug: fix leak.</li><li>42589340 - sparkplug: fix crash.</li></ul>\n\n[Compare with previous version](/wireshark/wireshark/-/merge_requests/3025/diffs?diff_id=186608853&start_sha=31074ceecc62cc76fab6c74e20531642aaf65423)",
          "author": {
            "id": 277876,
            "username": "crondaemon",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Dario Lombardo",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/143ae7a6f9e11c9eed24a7fdb44bb40d442fd274ba01a2e3a4abe1596819bea2?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/crondaemon"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-05-17T11:52:04.286Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-05-17T11:52:04.288Z",
          "system": true,
          "noteable_id": 100154947,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 3025,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "f270c1bca545a92f3979f01cd45738becbe52d31",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 576874452,
          "type": null,
          "body": "The g_strsplit is run on the data parameter, not the tvb contents.  As it currently stands, the sparkplugB dissector doesn't actually access the tvb at all, that's all done by the protobuf dissector.  The dissector does use the tvb as the \"anchor\" for the various elements added to the tree as there wasn't anywhere else to put them, but the string for those elements (data -> topic -> topic_elements) is actually parsed from the tvb by the MQTT dissector and not in the MQTT payload tvb handed to sparkplugB.\n\nI'm not suggesting that there shouldn't be a check on the minimum tvb length but it's not related to the topic string or any elements in it, but rather the messages that will be dissected by protobuf.  It's an odd situation, but if a dissector isn't dissecting any data from the tvb, just handing it off, should that dissector make minimum length checks?",
          "author": {
            "id": 6621762,
            "username": "graham.bloice",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Graham Bloice",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/8730bfac2267cb97ff1f8187d285f244745a03a783055c8fd6fcd679bfa71c6e?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/graham.bloice"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-05-17T12:13:04.815Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-05-17T12:13:04.815Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 100154947,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 3025,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c9c4ef806760ec613b1a7252e449a99c5c3ce2ba",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 576919101,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I looked into the code a bit deeper. The mqtt dissector is actually calling sparkplug with a null topic with the provided sample. The check then should be on `data`, assuming it's a string (indeed it is passed to a `g_str` function), and that would be strlen == 0. How does it sound?",
          "author": {
            "id": 277876,
            "username": "crondaemon",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Dario Lombardo",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/143ae7a6f9e11c9eed24a7fdb44bb40d442fd274ba01a2e3a4abe1596819bea2?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/crondaemon"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-05-17T12:48:55.553Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-05-17T12:50:07.505Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 100154947,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 3025,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "d4dce7224a67c463396d3350f158d1fed37ef0c6",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 576944957,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Data is an empty string, '\\0', or a NULL ptr? Looking at the blurb for g_strsplit(), there aren't any listed pre-conditions, but it does say that the string parameter is a pointer to a string and it will handle an empty string, so maybe just a check for data being a NULL?\n\nI'm not entirely sure what the blurb statement \"As a special case, the result of splitting the empty string \"\" is an empty vector, not a vector containing a single string\" means.  I took this to mean that the vector returns a NULL ptr, hence the existing check on topic_elements.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6621762,
            "username": "graham.bloice",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Graham Bloice",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/8730bfac2267cb97ff1f8187d285f244745a03a783055c8fd6fcd679bfa71c6e?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/graham.bloice"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-05-17T13:04:46.171Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-05-17T13:04:46.171Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 100154947,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 3025,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "6f9d54258759b60e778c280ec4424ab32cc3a231",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 576982635,
          "type": null,
          "body": "It's the empty string. However, despite `g_strsplit()` handles the empty string, `strcmp` forbids it. The solution looks to be a check on topic for NULL, and replace `strcmp` with `g_strcmp0`, that works.",
          "author": {
            "id": 277876,
            "username": "crondaemon",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Dario Lombardo",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/143ae7a6f9e11c9eed24a7fdb44bb40d442fd274ba01a2e3a4abe1596819bea2?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/crondaemon"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-05-17T13:37:22.234Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-05-17T13:37:22.234Z",
